    "added": "Nov 24, 2026, after review; post hoc, not part of the analysis fixed before the students ran",
    "why": "break_even reads only the failed test tasks a skill fixed, so failed skill runs, failed builds and builds that fixed nothing are left out of it; this block counts them",
    "definition": "per student, form and scenario with an attempted build, on the student's failed test tasks that the teacher passed: cost per use = mean over those tasks of (skill run cost, failed runs included, + that task's own rent cost if the skill did not fix it); uses to break even = build cost, all attempts / (mean rent cost - cost per use), or never if that saving is not positive; a failed build never pays back; a function's build cost is charged in full to each student",
